```cpp
#include <iostream>

void swap_ints(int* a, int* b) {
    int t = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = t;
}

int main() {
    int x = 1, y = 2;
    swap_ints(&x, &y);
    std::cout << x << ' ' << y << '\n';
}
```
The caller passes addresses with `&`; the function writes through them with `*`.

tasks.tests:
