```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <utility>

void reverse_range(int* first, int* last) {
    while (first != last && first != --last) {
        std::swap(*first, *last);
        ++first;
    }
}

int main() {
    int a[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
    reverse_range(a, a + 5);
    for (int x : a) std::cout << x << ' ';
    std::cout << '\n';
}
```
The condition first checks for an empty remaining range, then moves `last` onto a real element and stops if the two met in the middle.

tasks.tests:
